To execute a file ./filename.sh or sh filename.sh

The main purpose of linux is security.
Despite the fact that you created the file linux has to know who is allowed to execute a file,

Chmod - grants permissions 
ch stands for change
Chmod is divided into 3 categories:
1- which user has access
2- which group has access
3- what are your permissions

To grant access to everybody we use; chmod 777 filename.sh
7 for me, 7 for my group, 7 for everyone 

But why 777, Linux used a formala called 4 2 1 
4 - read
2 - write 

1 - execute

so the 7 means read, write and execute

